  "reason": "With no completed experiments, there is no evidence to guide exploitation, so the priority is establishing a clean, interpretable baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest and most standard configuration in the design space: it uses PCA (the most common and well-understood dimensionality reduction), a single profile (no aggregation complexity), and no image modality. This gives a clear reference performance against which every other design axis—multiprofile vs. singleprofile, alternative RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt), adding image data, and fusion strategy—can be meaningfully compared in subsequent experiments. Starting from the simplest RNA-only baseline maximizes the information gained per experiment because any future performance delta can be attributed to one specific design change rather than confounded by multiple simultaneous deviations from an unknown starting point."
}

